From b211c8c11951d0108c4b3a4f1b3fb55e1c253926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:10:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] popover: popover=hint gets its own stack

Hint popovers shared the auto popover stack, so showing a tooltip-style
hint popover closed an open auto popover menu. They now live in the
showing hint popover list with the document's hint stack parent, per the
current HTML spec: a hint popover closes other unrelated hint popovers
but leaves auto popovers open, an auto popover closes all hint popovers,
an auto popover opened from inside a hint popover is downgraded to hint,
and hiding the auto popover a hint stack hangs off hides that stack.
The topmost popover ancestor, hide popover stack until, hide popovers
until, light dismiss and popover stack position algorithms follow the
current spec text, which dialogs share. Results match Chrome step for
step on the hint repro.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
